# EmailJS public configuration.
# 1. Create a free account at https://www.emailjs.com
# 2. Add an email service that sends from your Gmail (codextech2025@gmail.com)
# 3. Create a template with these variables:
#    {{from_name}} {{from_email}} {{phone}} {{company}}
#    {{service}} {{budget}} {{message}} {{to_email}}
# 4. Set the template "To email" to codextech2025@gmail.com
#    and Reply To to {{from_email}}
# 5. Copy the Service ID, Template ID and Public Key below.
#
# Never add your EmailJS private key. Only the public key belongs in the frontend.
# Copy this file to .env and restart the dev server after changing it.
#
# If these values are empty, the form uses FormSubmit instead and emails
# codextech2025@gmail.com directly. FormSubmit sends a one-time confirmation
# email the first time an enquiry is submitted.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
